# Usage Guide: Assembly Algorithms

This guide details the technical workings and variable handling for the optimization of geometric compactness.

## Instance Configuration

The algorithm is driven through the `CONFIG` dictionary. Changing these values lets you adjust the complexity of the tiling problem.

|  Variable  | Type  | Description |
| :--------: | :---- | :---------- |
| `n_shapes` | `int` | Total number of polyominoes generated for the session.        |
| `min_size` | `int` | Minimum area of a piece (in grid units).        |
| `max_size` | `int` | Maximum area of a piece (in grid units).        |
| `seed`     | `int` | Seed used to fix the randomness and reproduce results. |


## Function Handling

